{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013CtLH8pkyW7ACoW1kKwZ8A","type":"tool_result","content":"165\tnode-72d14691\tstdout\t🚀 Server ready at: http://localhost:8080\n166\tnode-72d14691\tstdout\t⭐️ See sample requests: http://pris.ly/e/ts/rest-express#3-using-the-rest-api\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\t## Koyeb specific notes\n170\t\n171\t### Build\n172\t\n173\tBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `build` script, Koyeb automatically executes it after the dependencies installation.\n174\tIn the example, the `build` script is used to run `prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy && next build`.\n175\t\n176\t### Deployment\n177\t\n178\tBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `start` script, Koyeb automatically executes it to launch the application.\n179\tIn the example, the `start` script is used to run `node src/index.js`.\n180\t\n181\t### Database migrations and deployments\n182\t\n183\tIn the example you deployed, migrations are applied using the `prisma migrate deploy` command during the Koyeb build (as defined in the `build` script in `package.json`).\n184\t\n185\t### Additional notes\n186\t\n187\tIn this guide, we kept pre-set values for the region, instance size, and horizontal scaling. You can customize them according to your needs.\n188\t\n189\t> **Note:** The Ports section is used to let Koyeb know which port your application is listening to and properly route incoming HTTP requests. A default `PORT` environment variable is set to `8080` and incoming HTTP requests are routed to the `/` path when creating a new application.\n190\t> If your application is listening on another port, you can define another port to route incoming HTTP requests.\n191\t\n192\t## Summary\n193\t\n194\tCongratulations! You have successfully deployed a Node.js app with Prisma ORM to Koyeb.\n195\t\n196\tYou can find the source code for the example in [this GitHub repository](https://github.com/koyeb/example-prisma).\n197\t\n198\tFor more insight into Prisma Client's API, look at the route handlers in the `src/index.js` file.\n199\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ed60116-4216-427f-bae3-f4cbf4ebfd11","uuid":"3895efd6-9c66-434c-9aeb-a94058663285","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:31:08.208Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/t4/grep/src/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/deployment/traditional/deploy-to-koyeb.mdx","content":"node-72d14691\tstdout\t🚀 Server ready at: http://localhost:8080\nnode-72d14691\tstdout\t⭐️ See sample requests: http://pris.ly/e/ts/rest-express#3-using-the-rest-api\n```\n\n## Koyeb specific notes\n\n### Build\n\nBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `build` script, Koyeb automatically executes it after the dependencies installation.\nIn the example, the `build` script is used to run `prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy && next build`.\n\n### Deployment\n\nBy default, for applications using the Node.js runtime, if the `package.json` contains a `start` script, Koyeb automatically executes it to launch the application.\nIn the example, the `start` script is used to run `node src/index.js`.\n\n### Database migrations and deployments\n\nIn the example you deployed, migrations are applied using the `prisma migrate deploy` command during the Koyeb build (as defined in the `build` script in `package.json`).\n\n### Additional notes\n\nIn this guide, we kept pre-set values for the region, instance size, and horizontal scaling. You can customize them according to your needs.\n\n> **Note:** The Ports section is used to let Koyeb know which port your application is listening to and properly route incoming HTTP requests. A default `PORT` environment variable is set to `8080` and incoming HTTP requests are routed to the `/` path when creating a new application.\n> If your application is listening on another port, you can define another port to route incoming HTTP requests.\n\n## Summary\n\nCongratulations! You have successfully deployed a Node.js app with Prisma ORM to Koyeb.\n\nYou can find the source code for the example in [this GitHub repository](https://github.com/koyeb/example-prisma).\n\nFor more insight into Prisma Client's API, look at the route handlers in the `src/index.js` file.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":165,"totalLines":199}}}
